{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Introduce a sports fund for children from low-income households",
        "additional_details": "Over a third (34%) of UK parents said the cost of their children's participation in sport has had a significant impact on household finances, affecting their ability to pay for necessities such as bills and food.\r\n \r\nAs the cost of living continues to mean households need to cut back on outgoings, sports clubs and physical activity often fall victim. However, physical activity plays a vital role in supporting children\u2019s mental and physical wellbeing.",
        "background": "We would like the government to introduce financial support for children from low-income households who struggle to pay for costs such as club fees and equipment.",
